---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const evidence = '/api/v2/packages?monitor=security&search=observations&q=CVE-&include=security&detail=full&per_page=20';
const groupedURL = '/api/v2/packages?' + new URLSearchParams([
  ['AND-build:rva23', 'failed'], ['OR-build:rva23', 'unresolvable'], ['group', 'AND'],
  ['AND-maintenance', 'Advisory'], ['AND-maintenance', 'DepMismatch'], ['group', 'AND'],
]);
const batch = '/api/v2/packages:batchGet?names=bash&names=openssl&include=version&include=security';
---
<Base title="API">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>API</h1>
    <p>Read-only snapshots. <a href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI: parameters and response schemas</a>.</p>

    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">GET /api/v2</th><th scope="col">Returns</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/packages"><code>/packages</code></a></td>
          <td>Summaries + filter counts. <code>per_page</code>: default 100, max 200.
            <code>detail=full</code> adds evidence; requires <code>per_page≤20</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/packages/bash"><code>/packages/{'{name}'}</code></a></td>
          <td>Full package observations.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/packages:batchGet</code></td>
          <td>Full observations for 1–20 unique, repeated <code>names</code>, in request order.
            Any missing name fails the batch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/tracks/meson"><code>/tracks/{'{id}'}</code></a></td><td>Saved version-track observation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/targets"><code>/targets</code></a></td><td>OBS target identities.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/status"><code>/status</code></a></td><td>Collection freshness, coverage and errors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/api/v2/export"><code>/export</code></a></td><td>Complete snapshot, schema 2; unpaginated.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Queries</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>monitor</code> focuses filtering; repeated <code>include</code> selects returned monitors
        (default: all). IDs come from the list response's <code>monitors</code>.</li>
      <li><code>q</code> searches names; <code>search=observations</code> adds fact values,
        restricted by <code>monitor</code> when set. Matching is case-insensitive substring.</li>
      <li>Use ordered <code>AND-dimension=value</code>, <code>OR-dimension=value</code> and
        <code>NOT-dimension=value</code> parameters. Keep repeated keys in order.
        <code>group=AND</code>, <code>group=OR</code> or <code>group=NOT</code> seals preceding
        ungrouped conditions, using that operator to connect the whole group.
        Operations run left to right. Each expression starts from the scoped ALL,
        including inside groups: leading OR preserves ALL; leading NOT subtracts its operand;
        groups cannot nest. The response includes the normalized query and
        <code>query_node_limit</code> (conditions + group markers, before deduplication).</li>
      <li>Counts evaluate the complete expression after appending a candidate using
        <code>next_logic</code> (default <code>and</code>).
        Counts take the smaller of that result and the candidate's own scoped count, including selected choices, in every mode.
        <code>total</code> always counts the current expression; editing context does not change its results.
        OR deduplicates packages.
        Search stays in scope. Evidence views default to findings; <code>section=coverage</code>
        includes packages without findings. Check counts target coverage.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Build alternatives intersected with two alerts:</p>
    <pre><code>{groupedURL}</code></pre>
    <p><a href={groupedURL}>Run grouped query</a>. Dimensions use the monitor projection's IDs:
      <code>maintenance</code>, <code>buildsystem</code>, <code>build:TARGET</code>,
      <code>view</code>, <code>version_signal</code>, <code>requires</code>,
      <code>check:MONITOR</code>, <code>retained:MONITOR</code>.
      Malformed/over-budget queries return 422; no truncation or implicit exclusivity.</p>
    <p>Find advisory evidence:</p>
    <pre><code><a href={evidence}>{evidence}</a></code></pre>
    <p>Fetch known packages:</p>
    <pre><code><a href={batch}>{batch}</a></code></pre>

    <p><code>404</code> missing resource · <code>422</code> invalid package query · <code>503</code> no snapshot.<br />
      Preserve <code>check</code> and <code>stale</code>; null means unknown.
      One snapshot per response, not across pages.</p>
    <p><code>check.failures</code> identifies failed subchecks, including partial results.
      <code>check_groups</code> counts the <code>uncovered</code> and <code>failed</code> filters;
      <code>check_statuses</code> retains the individual states.</p>
    <p>Website display documents: <a href="/api/ui/packages">/api/ui/packages</a>,
      <a href="/api/ui/packages/bash">/api/ui/packages/{'{name}'}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
<style>
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; }
</style>
